<title>UK: BOE allots 170 million stg in repos to August 5.</title>
<headline>BOE allots 170 million stg in repos to August 5.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said that it provided the UK money market with 170 million stg of 6.75 percent repos to August 5.</p>
<p>This brought total liquidity provided to the market to 1.05 billion stg. The Bank revised its forecast for the liquidity shortage to 1.05 billion stg from the initial estimate of 850 million and the noon estimate of one billion stg.</p>
</text>
